Fix two-factor authentication

Discord rejects every 2FA code unless the login and the 2FA request carry an
X-Fingerprint; a rejected attempt can also sign the account out everywhere.
This is the cause of purple-discord issues #477 and #489, and the same fix
Discord Lite made in dosdude1/discord-lite@fde55a8.

- Before the password login, get a fingerprint from GET /experiments (falling
  back to POST /auth/fingerprint) and send it, with a login Referer, on the
  unauthenticated requests. Discord issues only 3 valid fingerprints per IP
  every 2 minutes (https://docs.discord.food/topics/experiments).
- Send the same login and 2FA bodies as the official client (undelete,
  login_source, gift_code_sku_id), and pass the login_instance_id from the
  login response on to the 2FA request.
- Send 8-character backup codes to /auth/mfa/backup instead of /auth/mfa/totp,
  without the dash they are displayed with.
- Word the prompt after the methods the login response says the account has
  (totp, backup), so eg. an account without an authenticator app asks for a
  backup code instead of silently rejecting authenticator codes.
- Report Discord's own error message (eg. "Invalid two-factor code") instead
  of "Bad username/password".
- Redact the 2FA request bodies (code and ticket) in the debug log.
- Free fingerprint, mfa_ticket and login_instance_id on close.

